# Hawk APL style 100mm 2x
#
# Front anamorphic made by lenses/make_anamorphic.py from
#   lens_files/Leica_100mm_(Leica_Summilux_C_100mm_T1.4).lens
# scaled to 100mm, with the iris set to f/3 (the stop of the reference footage).
# A Galilean cylindrical attachment (BK7 glass, coating 1) in front of the
# original lens.  Horizontal field 2x wider (squeeze 2x paraxial), vertical
# unchanged; focal_length below is the vertical (taking lens) focal length.
# The attachment's apertures are 1.5x make_anamorphic.py's default so
# off-axis ghosts are not clipped.
# NOT a Vantage Hawk prescription (none is public).  A stand-in for flare
# work, tuned against Hawk APL test footage: faint lavender streak, large red-
# pink oval ghost below the light, soft glow.
# See looks/Hawk_APL_Style_100mm_2x.json for the matching look.

name: Hawk APL style 100mm 2x
focal_length: 100

surfaces:
# radius     thickness   ior      abbe   semi_ap   coating  type
# --- Front anamorphic attachment: 2x squeeze, cylinder axes vertical ---
  -106.978  3.000  1.51680  64.2  104.0550  1  cyl_y   # plano-concave cylinder, F = -207
  0  191.270  1.00000  0.0  104.0550  1   # flat back, air gap (solved: afocal)
  0  20.860  1.51680  64.2  130.0650  1   # flat front of the positive cylinder
  -213.955  15.000  1.00000  0.0  130.0650  1  cyl_y   # plano-convex cylinder, F = +414
